    <DataNode elementId="NITRATE" textLabel="nitrate" type="Metabolite">
      <Xref identifier="NHNBFGGVMKEFGY-UHFFFAOYSA-N" dataSource="InChIKey" />
      <Graphics centerX="1062.6973876953125" centerY="1026.698974609375" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="xue, PMN, nilo-poyanco">Nitrate is the conjugate base of |FRAME: CPD-15028|. It is a common electron acceptor for anaerobic bacteria (see |FRAME: Nitrate-Reduction &quot;nitrate reduction pathways&quot;|), and is also the ultimate product of an ammonia oxidation process known as |FRAME: P282-PWY nitrification|.</Comment>
